{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "DOfUnsupported",
    "description": "esm-spec §4.2, REFUSE half: a right-hand-side structural D over a shape outside the closed set the tendency resolution differentiates. `^` is evaluable-core arithmetic and sits immediately beside the operators that ARE covered (`+ - neg * /`), which is what makes it the sharp boundary case: it needs the power RULE, not a substitution, so the resolution answers nothing and the node must be refused rather than given a value.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciAST conformance"],
    "created": "2026-09-08T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": ["conformance", "esm-spec-4.2", "unlowered-operator", "refusal"]
  },
  "models": {
    "M": {
      "variables": {
        "x": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg", "default": 2.0, "description": "Exponentially decaying state" },
        "k": { "type": "parameter", "units": "1/s", "default": 3.0, "description": "Decay rate" },
        "dsq": { "type": "unknown", "units": "kg^2/s", "description": "D of x^2 — outside the differentiable set" }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["x"], "wrt": "t" },
          "rhs": { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["k"] }, "x"] }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "The chain rule this format defines covers `+ - neg * /` and nothing else. `x^2` would need 2*x*dx/dt — a differentiation RULE for `^`, not a substitution — so the node resolves to nothing and §4.2 requires a refusal. The mathematically intended value is 2*2*(-6) = -24; the value the pre-fix evaluators returned was 0. Both are forbidden.",
          "lhs": "dsq",
          "rhs": { "op": "D", "args": [{ "op": "^", "args": ["x", 2] }], "wrt": "t" }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "d_of_unsupported_is_refused",
          "description": "The run must be refused rather than answered. `expected` is deliberately 0 — the very value the pre-fix evaluators returned for EVERY unresolvable D — so a binding that invents one passes on the arithmetic and is caught only by the outcome class.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 1.0 },
          "assertions": [
            { "variable": "dsq", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.0, "tolerance": { "abs": 1e-9 } }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "domain": { "temporal": {} }
}
